From 5bf28f196a191986c6816bb3670cc9b311221c0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:27:24 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 80/81] render: skinned and morphed 3D models, posed by their
 animation layers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A model object with an MDLS skeleton and MDLA animations now reads `animationlayers` (as an
image's puppet does) and is posed every frame with the puppet's clock, weight and mixing (GH
0x1401d4d00, 0x140291f60, 0x140228470). Its meshes draw on the GPU as WE does:

- SKINNING with BONECOUNT = the bone count (GH 0x140230ec0 sets both for a skinned mesh), the
  per-vertex a_BlendIndices (uvec4) and a_BlendWeights, and g_Bones = world (pose) · bindWorld⁻¹
  as mat4x3, uploaded per draw. A mesh whose weights are all zero isn't skinned.
- MORPHING (MORPHING_NORMALS with the mesh's flag 0x400) over a morph map in g_Texture5 (the
  casters' g_Texture1), in model_vertex_v1.h's layout: per target, per vertex 3 (6) floats at
  (gl_VertexID + g_MorphOffsets[1 + t]) · 3 packed into a square RGBA texture; g_MorphWeights[0]
  is the position scale (2.8.42's MORPH_POSITION_SCALE), the snorm deltas the texels. A vertex's
  point is its vec4 position's w − 1, else its own index. The weights come from the animations'
  blend-shape tracks.
- The shadow casters get the same combos, bones and map.

Inferred: which 11 targets are drawn when more are weighted (ours: the first 11 with a weight),
and the morph map's half-float storage (WE's 2.8.485 reads a snorm16 buffer). No library model
has a skeleton or blend shapes; the checks are synthetic. rootmotion and the IModelLayer script
API (getAnimationLayer … on a model) are not done.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-coverage.md F4 (skinned / animated 3D models)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
